            <div xml:id="d534">

                <pb facs="0517" n="505" sameAs="frus:frus1940v01/pg505"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">764.71/279: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Rumania</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gunther</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bucharest</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-09-06T20:00:00+02:00">September 6,
                            1940—8 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 7—10:38 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>509. My 497, September 5, 5 p.m.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d534-f1"/> A high official
                    who had been in constant touch with the Transylvanian development has confided
                    to me that Rumania was forced into acceptance of the Axis dictate by dire
                    threats of Axis support to Hungary and subsequent partition of Rumania into
                    zones of influence between Germany and Russia. It was made clear by inference
                    that Germany and Russia were working together in this instance. Further, that
                    Italy had insisted upon “getting something out of all this” which was to have
                    Hungary grateful principally to her.</p>
                <p>I am further informed that Hungary no longer desires to proceed on the principle
                    of transfers of population as provided in the agreement since she fears many
                    racial Hungarians would not opt for Hungarian nationality. This change in
                    procedure has German concurrence.</p>
                <p>Even more troops are being hurried to the Hungarian boundary.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gunther</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
